# Files are LF, in the repo and on disk, so scripted edits match on every machine. Only Windows batch
# files keep CRLF. See REDnode's CLAUDE.md, "Writing files on this PC (Windows, Git Bash, PowerShell 5.1)".
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Every change adds a line under Unreleased, so two branches always touch the same spot. Union keeps
# both sides when git merges them; check the result for group headings run together.
CHANGELOG.md merge=union
